From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: rtl8365mb: wait out the full chip reset time

The reset bit clears well before the RTL8365MB/RTL8367S has finished its
internal bring-up, so configuring it right away makes register writes to
blocks that are not up yet get lost. The switch is then left half
configured: the CPU port link comes up and the switch still transmits
towards the CPU, but nothing the CPU sends is ever forwarded - no MIB TX
counter moves on any user port, while the MAC reports every frame as
transmitted without errors.

Seen on a TP-Link Archer AX55 v1 (IPQ5018 + RTL8367S, 2.5G HSGMII trunk)
on roughly three out of four boots. Unbinding and rebinding the driver
always fixed it at runtime. With this patch: 6 out of 6 clean boots.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
@@ -2981,6 +2981,7 @@ static int rtl8365mb_switch_init(struct
 static int rtl8365mb_reset_chip(struct realtek_priv *priv)
 {
 	u32 val;
+	int ret;
 
 	priv->write_reg_noack(priv, RTL8365MB_CHIP_RESET_REG,
 			      FIELD_PREP(RTL8365MB_CHIP_RESET_HW_MASK, 1));
@@ -2989,9 +2990,23 @@ static int rtl8365mb_reset_chip(struct r
 	 * for 100 ms before accessing any registers to prevent ACK timeouts.
 	 */
 	msleep(100);
-	return regmap_read_poll_timeout(priv->map, RTL8365MB_CHIP_RESET_REG, val,
-					!(val & RTL8365MB_CHIP_RESET_HW_MASK),
-					20000, 1e6);
+	ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(priv->map, RTL8365MB_CHIP_RESET_REG, val,
+				       !(val & RTL8365MB_CHIP_RESET_HW_MASK),
+				       20000, 1e6);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* The reset bit clears well before the chip has finished its internal
+	 * bring-up. Configuring it too early makes register writes to blocks
+	 * that are not up yet get lost, which leaves the switch in a
+	 * half-configured state: the CPU port link comes up and the switch
+	 * still transmits towards the CPU, but nothing the CPU sends is ever
+	 * forwarded (no MIB TX counters move on any user port). Honour the
+	 * full reset time the documentation asks for.
+	 */
+	msleep(900);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int rtl8365mb_setup(struct dsa_switch *ds)
